      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BIDEN TIME (3) is the one to beat after justifying odds-on support in a BM58 at this track, beating NEW ENTERPRISE by a length and adding another strong track-and-distance result to his record. The rise to BM64 is the obvious new task, but Jarrod Todd and Gary Clarke bring leading local profiles and the gelding has won four times at around 1600m. SASS (6) has the sharper last-start margin, having beaten I'M A Dreamer by just over three lengths in a BM58, and her record with Billy Cray gives that win extra substance. CANGGU (8) was only two lengths from BIDEN TIME last start and has two wins and three placings from eight starts at the distance, so he is a genuine danger if he holds that level. I'M A DREAMER (7) was safely held by SASS but remains honest, has extensive mile form, and his season record keeps him in the minor-money mix.",
